explanation:
Net new equity = Common stock_{end} – Common stock_{beg} 
 Common stock + Retained earnings = Total owners’ equity
 Net new equity = (OE – RE)_{end} – (OE – RE)_{beg} 
 Net new equity = OE_{end} – OE_{beg} + RE_{beg} – RE_{end} 
 RE_{end} = RE_{beg} + Additions to RE
 So: Net new equity = OE_{end} – OE_{beg} + RE_{beg} – (RE_{beg} + Additions to RE) = OE_{end} – OE_{beg} – Additions to RE
 Net new equity = $42,677 – 42,124 – 1,182.98 = –$629.98

 Cash flow to stockholders = Dividends – Net new equity 
 Cash flow to stockholders = $1,261– (–$629.98) 
 Cash flow to stockholders = $1,890.98
